 both left–right and up–down, but the axes are **off-centre**:\n\n- column x mirrors to column 31−x, and row y mirrors to row 31−y;\n- the centre of symmetry therefore lies between indices 15 and 16, not at 14.5.\n\nAs a result, the first two rows and columns (x < 2, y < 2) have no mirror partner inside the grid.\n\n## Step 1: restore from horizontal and vertical reflections\n\nThe axes are found from the grid instead of being hard-coded. For each candidate axis position `a`, we compare row or column pairs `(a−1−j, a+j)` and ignore any cell that is 9. A candidate is accepted if no pair disagrees. Among the accepted candidates we pick the one closest to the centre.\n\nEach 9-cell then has up to three partners:\n\n- (y, 2·ax−1−x)\n- (2·ay−1−y, x)\n- (2·ay−1−y, 2·ax−1−x)\n\nWe take the value of any partner that is in-bounds and not 9. In a consistent pattern all such partners agree, and the reference raises an error if they don't. This step alone repairs all four demonstrations.\n\n## Step 2: residual cells via the diagonal\n\nLook at the test input. The 9 block covers rows 0–7 and columns 12–18.\n\n- Its horizontal mirror, columns 13–19, is mostly 9 itself.\n- Rows 0–1 mirror to rows 31 and 30, which are outside the grid.\n\nSo cells such as (0,13)–(0,18) have no usable horizontal or vertical partner. For these, the reference uses the pattern's **diagonal** symmetry about the same centre: cell (y, x) corresponds to (x+ay−ax, y+ax−ay), together with that cell's horizontal and vertical mirrors.\n\nThe fact sheet rates the plain transpose as weak, at 50–60% agreement. That is honest caution: across the whole grid the diagonal holds less strictly than the two mirrors. This is the main uncertain assumption. The reference only falls back to the diagonal for cells that step 1 couldn't fill, and it requires exactly one consistent value, otherwise it raises an error. None of the train pairs needs this step; it exists for the test input's corner block.\n\n## Checkpoints\n\n1. Canvas after the horizontal/vertical reflection repair.\n2. If any 9s remain, the canvas after the diagonal completion. When no 9s remain, the first canvas is already the final answer and is not emitted twice.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n\n    def axis(size, vertical):\n        possible = []\n        for a in range(1, size):\n            ok = True\n            for j in range(min(a, size - a)):\n                p, q = a - 1 - j, a + j\n                u, v = (g[:, p], g[:, q]) if vertical else (g[p, :], g[q, :])\n                known = (u != 9) & (v != 9)\n                if np.any(u[known] != v[known]):\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            if ok:\n                possible.append(a)\n        if not possible:\n            raise ValueError('No reflection axis')\n        return min(possible, key=lambda a: (abs(2 * a - size), a))\n\n    ax, ay = axis(W, True), axis(H, False)\n    out = g.copy()\n    for y in range(H):\n        for x in range(W):\n            if g[y, x] != 9:\n                continue\n            partners = [(y, 2 * ax - 1 - x), (2 * ay - 1 - y, x), (2 * ay - 1 - y, 2 * ax - 1 - x)]\n            values = {int(g[a, b]) for a, b in partners\n                      if 0 <= a < H and 0 <= b < W and g[a, b] != 9}\n            if len(values) > 1:\n                raise ValueError('Inconsistent reflection evidence')\n            if values:\n                out[y, x] = values.pop()\n    emit(out, 'Restore occluded (9) cells from their left-right and up-down mirror partners about the inferred off-centre symmetry axes.')\n\n    partial = out.copy()\n    changed = False\n    for y in range(H):\n        for x in range(W):\n            if partial[y, x] != 9:\n                continue\n            yy, xx = x + ay - ax, y + ax - ay\n            partners = [(yy, xx), (yy, 2 * ax - 1 - xx), (2 * ay - 1 - yy, xx), (2 * ay - 1 - yy, 2 * ax - 1 - xx)]\n            values = {int(partial[a, b]) for a, b in partners\n                      if 0 <= a < H and 0 <= b < W and partial[a, b] != 9}\n            if len(values) != 1:\n                raise ValueError('Diagonal completion is absent or ambiguous')\n            out[y, x] = values.pop()\n            changed = True\n    if changed:\n        emit(out, 'Fill the remaining occluded cells (those whose mirror partners were off-grid or also hidden) using the diagonal reflection of the same centred pattern.')\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each pattern is mirror symmetric both left–right and up–down, but the axes are **off-centre**:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- column x mirrors to column 31−x, and row y mirrors to row 31−y;"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- the centre of symmetry therefore lies between indices 15 and 16, not at 14.5."}],"repair":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"## Step 1: restore from horizontal and vertical reflections"},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Restore occluded (9) cells from their left-right and up-down mirror partners about the inferred off-centre symmetry axes."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Fill the remaining occluded cells (those whose mirror partners were off-grid or also hidden) using the diagonal reflection of the same centred pattern."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The reference only falls back to the diagonal for cells that step 1 couldn't fill, and it requires exactly one consistent value, otherwise it raises an error."}],"layers":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Restore occluded (9) cells from their left-right and up-down mirror partners about the inferred off-centre symmetry axes."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Fill the remaining occluded cells (those whose mirror partners were off-grid or also hidden) using the diagonal reflection of the same centred pattern."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":true,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":true},"artifact_sha256":"f2a3dd1f16196374f6a808152c0a550f38a0a3a6cce5006ca02eb4bc015f4174","task_sha256":"bc027351322466deb138787238238d2c8f0441267a10f85a64f6d4351c5ecea8","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
